1. What this covers

"The Software" means WoundCarePro: the application and the server, their source code and
documentation, and every installer and update built from them. The drawings of the human
body are dealt with in section 7.

2. What is published, and why

Installers and update packages of the Software are published in the releases of the
repository https://github.com/BlackDragdroit/WoundCarePro, so that installed copies can
fetch their updates. Publishing them grants no rights in the Software. The Software is not
open source. Its source code is not published and is confidential.

3. No rights without permission

No right to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell or host the
Software, or to make works derived from it, in whole or in part, is granted, except as
stated in sections 4 and 5.

4. Who may use the Software

The Software may be installed and used only by persons and organisations to whom the
copyright holder has given permission, and only within the terms agreed with them. That
permission is not transferable.

5. What is allowed without asking

- Viewing the public repository named in section 2, and forking it on GitHub, to the
  extent that GitHub's Terms of Service give every GitHub user that right for a public
  repository. A fork stays subject to this licence.
- What applicable law permits regardless of a licence and does not allow a licence to
  exclude.

6. Components by others

The Software contains components by others, among them React, Tauri, jsPDF, JSZip, Lucide,
Express, mysql2, the typeface Google Sans Flex and the DejaVu fonts. Each of them stays
under its own licence (MIT, ISC, BSD, Apache 2.0, MPL 2.0, zlib, SIL Open Font License,
the DejaVu fonts licence). This licence does not apply to them and limits no right those
licences grant.

7. The drawings of the human body

The drawings of the human body that the Software contains were bought by the copyright
holder and are used in the Software under the terms of that purchase. The rights in them
stay with their author. Nothing in this file licenses them to anyone: they may not be
taken from the Software, copied, or used elsewhere.

8. Data recorded with the Software

Data that users record with the Software is theirs. This licence gives the copyright holder
no rights in it.

9. No warranty, liability

To the extent that applicable law permits, the Software is provided "as is", without
warranty of any kind, and the copyright holder is not liable for damage that arises from
its use. Liability that the law does not allow to be excluded, for example for intent, for
gross negligence or for injury to life, body or health, is unaffected. An agreement with a
permitted user may provide otherwise.

The Software is a tool for documentation. It does not replace professional judgement.

10. Requests

Requests for permission go to the copyright holder:
https://github.com/BlackDragdroit

